$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }x\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{14})+(\goldD{-4})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{5}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $f(\blueD{5})$:

$\begin{align}
f(\blueD{5})&=(\blueD{5})^2-10(\blueD{5})-56
\\\\
&=25-50-56
\\\\
&=-81
\end{align}$
